course: dictionary
lesson: 9783
title: Capital letters and place names
level: primary-6
stars: 2
explain: A capital letter at the start of a word often marks a special name, such as a person, a day or a place. «In the poem, Kipling places the story on Merrow Down near Guildford in Surrey, England.» Surrey has a capital S because it is the name of a place, a county in the south-east of England.
explain: The same spelling can also be a common word with a small letter. A surrey, with a small s, is an old-fashioned light carriage pulled by a horse. Context tells you which one is meant. «Lottie lives in a big house in Surrey» is about a place, because you live in a house, and you do not ride in one.
explain: Ask yourself: is this word describing a place on a map, or a thing you could ride in? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense. If the sentence says the story happens near the River Wey, then Surrey must be a place.
fact: Surrey, with a capital S, is a county in the south-east of England, next to London.
fact: A surrey, with a small s, is an old-fashioned light, four-wheeled carriage pulled by a horse.
fact: A surrey has two seats and sometimes a fringed roof on top.
fact: A surrey is mostly an American word, and it is rare today.
fact: «The First Letter and the Alphabet stories happen in Surrey, south of London, near Guildford and the River Wey.» Here the capital S shows that Surrey is a place.
exercise: «The First Letter and the Alphabet stories happen in Surrey, south of London.» What is Surrey here? | A carriage with two seats | A kind of horse | *A place, a county south of London | A river that flows into the Thames
exercise: An old story says, «They rode to the market in a surrey with a fringe on top.» What is a surrey? | A big ship with sails | A type of bread | *A small, light carriage pulled by a horse | A county next to London
exercise: «Lottie lives in a big house in Surrey.» What does the capital S tell you? | The house is very old | *Surrey is the name of a place | Lottie is a horse | Surrey is a kind of carriage
test: «In the poem, Kipling places the story on Merrow Down near Guildford in Surrey, England.» Where is Merrow Down? | In a big house in Lottie's garden | On a ship at sea | *Near Guildford in Surrey, England | In the middle of London
test: Which sentence uses a place name? | «Her surrey was painted bright blue.» | «The horse pulled the cart up the hill.» | *«Lottie lives in a big house in Surrey.» | «The old surrey had a fringed roof.»
exam: Ella reads, «The surrey stopped outside the inn.» What is a surrey here? | A type of cloud | A kind of river | A county in England | *A light carriage pulled by a horse
